      "writtenOn": "2022-10-20T23:12:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please consider using a \u0027@nullable Int\u0027 and getting rid of the boolean above. Also, what does \u0027stereoPosition\u0027 mean?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "385df3f8cf3ee5a74e84dfc8c38a27c3f7beb2fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b29e4d68_6e976297",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/android/hardware/audio/effect/Volume.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T20:43:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m actually not quite sure about using @nullable in this case.\nWith @nullable we are using a nullopt to imply disable and actual value to imply enable, which IMO doesn\u0027t give a clear interface definition. Usually when something is disabled, the original value was kept and took affect when it\u0027s re-enabled, now we are requesting client to pass the value every time.\nFrom implementation point of view, it\u0027s adding little more requirement to the validation/checking for nullopt.\n\nNot sure if this make sense, happy to learn more thoughts from you, thanks.\n\n\nRegarding stereoPosition, from existing code it\u0027s trying to put some weight between L/R channel, but seems we don\u0027t use them now, so will remove it.",
      "parentUuid": "6085815a_2d3ba3a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 23
      },
